Wait — but is a comma before a new clause keyword (SET/REMOVE/ADD/DELETE) invalid in real DynamoDB? Yes — commas separate actions within a section only. E.g. "SET a = :x, REMOVE b" is invalid in real DynamoDB ("Syntax error; token: \"REMOVE\", near: \", REMOVE\""). And `UpdateExpressionSetActionParser.is_possible_start` → `UpdateExpressionPathParser.is_possible_start(token)` — check what that returns for "REMOVE" (a reserved keyword). If it returns True for any ATTRIBUTE token including reserved keywords, then "SET a=:x, REMOVE b" currently gets parsed as set action with path "REMOVE"... Actually then the validator might complain. Let me check UpdateExpressionPathParser.is_possible_start.

